{
"i": 190,
"where": "スライド10",
"en": "Both cdecl and stdcall conventions perform explicit stack frame linkage",
"ja": ""
},
{
"i": 191,
"where": "スライド10",
"en": "Each time you enter a new function, the old ebp (\"stack frame base pointer\" by Intel convention) gets pushed onto the stack, and the new esp (top-of-the stack pointer, which now points at the copy of ebp), gets moved into ebp",
"ja": ""
},
